---Creates a skill from markdown instructions, or turns an existing canvas the caller owns into a skill.
---
---Required scopes — bot: `skills:write`; user: `skills:write`
---
---Rate limit tier: 2
---
---Method-specific errors (the `error` slug on the SlackError):
---  - `invalid_arguments` — The arguments are invalid, for example both or neither of `instructions` and `canvas_id` were sent.
---  - `canvas_not_found` — The canvas doesn't exist or the caller can't see it.
---  - `not_canvas_owner` — Only the canvas owner can turn it into a skill.
---  - `is_a_template` — Canvas templates can't be turned into skills.
---  - `already_a_skill` — The canvas is already a skill. Use `slackbot.skills.update` to change it.
---  - `invalid_category` — `category` isn't one of the skill categories.
---  - `display_name_too_long` — `display_name` is longer than 255 characters.
---  - `description_too_long` — `description` is longer than 400 characters.
---  - `example_prompt_too_long` — `example_prompt` is longer than 200 characters.
---  - `instructions_too_large` — `instructions` is larger than 500,000 bytes.
---  - `too_many_mcp_servers` — More apps were declared than the caller can enable at once.
---  - `mcp_server_not_found` — One or more declared apps don't exist or aren't available to the caller. `invalid_mcp_servers` lists them.
---  - `restricted_action` — The caller isn't allowed to author skills.
---  - `feature_not_enabled` — The Skills API isn't enabled for this organization.
---  - `canvas_disabled_user_team` — Canvases are disabled for the caller's team.
---  - `free_teams_cannot_create_standalone_canvases` — Free teams can't create standalone canvases.
---  - `canvas_editing_locked` — Another edit to the canvas is in progress. Retry the request.
---  - `canvas_creation_failed` — The skill's canvas couldn't be created.
---  - `internal_error` — The skill couldn't be saved. Retry the request.
---
---See https://docs.slack.dev/reference/methods/slackbot.skills.create
---
